  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Gender Equality and Women`s and Girls` Empowerment in Food Security and Nutrition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activities will contribute to increase awareness, knowledge and skills on the CFS Voluntary Guidelines on Gender Equality and Women&apos;s and Girls&apos; Empowerment in the context of Food Security and Nutrition (VG-GEWGE) and to create knowledge products and tools that can utilized by member states and other key stakeholders, including civil society, to promote the uptake of the Guidelines. In this regard, the activities directly contribute to FAO Strategic Framework, notably BL1 on Gender equality and women?s empowerment, and to SDGs targets, and are in line with Colombia and Kenya?s Country Programming Frameworks (CPFs).</narrative>
  </description>
